	"Actor-SAB-Attributes2": "• Detects cloaked ground units and spies\n• Infiltrates production buildings to steal technology\n    • Allies: Cryo Mortar, Reckoner, Phantom\n    • Soviets: Cyberdog, Cyclops, Kamov\n    • GDI: Sonic Mortar, Basilisk, Shade\n    • Nod: Chem Mortar, Mantis, Vertigo\n    • Scrin: Cyberscrin, Viper, Manticore\n• Infiltrates radars/tech centers to lock technology\n• Infiltrates any building for vision",
	"Actor-SBAG-Description2": "• Stops infantry and light vehicles\n• Can be crushed by tanks",
	"Actor-SCOL-Attributes2": "• Requires power to operate\n• Detects cloaked units",
	"Actor-SEAL-Attributes2": "• Detects spies\n• Plants C4 to destroy structures",
	"Actor-SEEK-Attributes2": "• Detects cloaked units, spies and submarines\n• Can traverse water",
	"Actor-SGEN-Attributes2": "• Maximum 1 can be built\n• Cloaks nearby units and structures\n• Requires power to operate\n• Special Ability: Tiberium Stealth",
	"Actor-SGEN-Description2": "Makes units/structures invisible.",
	"Actor-SHAD-Attributes2": "• Cloaked when not in combat\n• Shadow beacons provide vision and attach to enemy vehicles that pass over them\n• Detects cloaked ground units and spies\n• Special Ability: Shadow Beacon",
	"Actor-SHAD-Description2": "Stealth infantry armed with a machine pistol and grenades.",
	"Actor-SHAD-Weaknesses2": "• Weak vs Heavy Armor\n• Cannot attack Aircraft\n• Has difficulty hitting moving vehicles",
	"Actor-SHAR-Attributes2": "• Requires power to operate\n• Detects cloaked aircraft",
	"Actor-SIGN-Attributes2": "• Maximum 1 can be built\n• Cannot be captured or hacked",
	"Actor-SMCV-Attributes2": "• Special Ability: Deploy into Colony Platform\n• Can traverse water",
	"Actor-SNIP-Attributes2": "• Camouflaged when not moving\n• When elite, kills crew of vehicles with less than 50% HP",
	"Actor-SNIP-Weaknesses2": "• Weak vs Buildings, Defenses\n• Cannot attack aircraft",
	"Actor-SPEN-Description2": "Produces and repairs\nsubmarines and transports.",
	"Actor-SPY-Attributes2": "• Disguise as enemy infantry by right-clicking them\n• Detects cloaked ground units and spies\n • Infiltration effects:\n    • Power Plants: Power outage\n    • Barracks/Factory: Infantry/vehicles produced as veteran\n    • Superweapons: Reset timer\n    • Radar: Reset shroud\n    • Helipad: Single-use paratroopers\n    • Airfield/Gravity Stabilizer: Single-use airstrike",
	"Actor-SPY-GenericName": "Soldier",
	"Actor-SREP-Attributes2": "• Nearby helipads/airfields will repair landed aircraft\n• Can retrofit existing units with upgrades",
	"Actor-STLK-Attributes2": "• Special Ability: Cloak\n• Moves faster while cloaked\n• Briefly takes greatly reduced damage after decloaking",
	"Actor-SUK-Weaknesses2": "• Weak vs Infantry, Buildings\n• Cannot attack Aircraft",
	"Actor-SUK.SEISMIC-Description": "Fast ground attack aircraft armed with powerful explosive munitions.",
	"Actor-SUK.SEISMIC-Strengths": "• Strong vs Buildings, Heavy Armor, Defenses, Light Armor",
	"Actor-SUK.SEISMIC-Weaknesses": "• Weak vs Infantry\n• Cannot attack Aircraft\n• Has difficulty hitting moving targets",
	"Actor-SWAL-Description2": "• Stops units\n• Blocks enemy fire\n• Regenerates over time",
	"Actor-SYRD-Description2": "Produces and repairs\nships and transports.",
	"Actor-SYRD.gdi-Description2": "Produces and repairs ships\nand transports.",
	"Actor-TDOG-Attributes2": "• Detects cloaked units, spies and mines\n• Detects the scent of enemy vehicles beyond vision range\n• Immune to mind control\n• Explodes on death or on contact with a target",
	"Actor-THF-Attributes2": "• Cloaked with increased vision when not moving",
	"Actor-THWK-Weaknesses2": "• Cannot attack Aircraft\n• Has difficulty hitting moving targets\n• Cannot fire while moving\n• Rockets can be shot down by static anti-air defenses",
	"Actor-TIGR-Weaknesses2": "• Weak vs Infantry, Defenses, Buildings\n• Cannot acquire targets at close range",
	"Actor-TITN-Attributes2": "• Can crush smaller vehicles and concrete walls\n• Self repairs to 50% out of combat",
	"Actor-TMPL-Attributes2": "• Requires power to operate\n• Special Ability: Cluster Missile",
	"Actor-TMPP-Attributes2": "• Maximum 1 can be built\n• Cannot be captured or hacked\n• Can convert regular infantry to cyborgs",
	"Actor-TNKD-Weaknesses2": "• Weak vs Infantry, Buildings, Defenses, Light Armor\n• Cannot attack Aircraft",
	"Actor-TPOD-Attributes2": "• Can crush concrete walls\n• Self repairs on Tiberium or other resources when not in combat",
	"Actor-TPWR-Attributes": "• Boosts nearby Tesla Coils",
	"Actor-TRAN-Attributes2": "• Can carry infantry\n• Can Paradrop infantry (Force Fire)",
	"Actor-TRPC-Attributes2": "• Empowers nearby basic infantry\n• Heals all nearby infantry\n• Detects cloaked units and mines",
	"Actor-TSLA-Attributes2": "• Requires power to operate\n• Detects cloaked units\n• Can be buffed or made work during low power by Shock Troopers",
	"Actor-ToxicCloud-Name": "(support power)",
	"Actor-U3-Attributes2": "• Deploys for personal anti-tank fortification\n• Uncrushable when deployed",
	"Actor-U3-Weaknesses2": "• Weak vs Infantry, Light Armor\n• Weak anti-infantry weapon when not deployed",
	"Actor-V3RL-Weaknesses2": "• Cannot attack Aircraft\n• Has difficulty hitting moving targets\n• Rockets can be shot down by static anti-air defenses",
	"Actor-VSPK-Attributes2": "• Corrupts resources\n• Damages nearby enemies over time\n• Direct damage is reflected back to the attacker",
	"Actor-Veil-Name": "(Veil of War)",
	"Actor-WCHR-Attributes2": "• Can attach parasites to enemy vehicles & structures\n• Cloaked with increased vision when not moving\n• Detects cloaked ground units and spies\n• Applies multi-target suppression (Collector-73 only)\n• Special Ability: Teleport (with upgrade)",
	"Actor-WEAT-Attributes2": "• Maximum 1 can be built\n• Requires power to operate\n• Special Ability: Lightning Storm",
	"Actor-WTNK-Attributes2": "• Briefly disables vehicles/defenses\n• Kills crew of vehicles with less than 50% HP (with upgrade)\n• Crewless vehicles capturable by infantry",
	"Actor-World-MPStartUnits_heavyallies-ClassName": "Heavy Support",
	"Actor-World-MPStartUnits_heavysoviet-ClassName": "Heavy Support",
	"Actor-World-MPStartUnits_lightallies-ClassName": "Light Support",
	"Actor-World-MPStartUnits_lightsoviet-ClassName": "Light Support",
	"Actor-World-MPStartUnits_mcvonly-ClassName": "MCV Only",
	"Actor-YURI-Attributes2": "• Maximum 1 can be trained\n• Detects cloaked ground units and spies\n• Immune to mind control\n• Shorter range and longer reload against vehicles\n• Psychic detection radius\n• Special Ability: Mind Blast",
	"Actor-ZRAI-Attributes2": "• Shots reduce enemy movement and rate of fire\n• Special Ability: Jump-Pack",
	"Actor-abur.upgrade-Description2": "Equips Orcas, Orca Bombers and Hover Mammoths with afterburners.\n\nUpgrades: Orca\nUpgrades: Orca Bomber\nUpgrades: Hover Mammoth",
	"Actor-advart.upgrade-Description2": "Enable Scrin infantry to move faster.\n\nUpgrades: Scrin Infantry",
	"Actor-airborne.upgrade-Description2": "Improved training and logistics for airborne troops, resulting in greater effectiveness and faster preparation.\n\nUpgrades: Airdrop: Guardian GIs\nUpgrades: Airdrop: Grizzly Tanks",
	"Actor-airborne.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Airborne units have veterancy\n+ Airborne units take 25% less time to prepare",
	"Actor-allegiance.upgrade-Description2": "Upgrade depends on chosen allegiance.\n\n• Loyalist: Eviscerator research\n• Rebel: Impaler research\n• Malefic: Stalker research",
	"Actor-apb.upgrade-Description2": "Upgrades Snipers granting them Raufoss armor piercing rounds, which stun and damage vehicles.\n\nUpgrades: Sniper",
	"Actor-apoc.upgrade-Description2": "Allows production of Apocalypse Tanks.\n\nReplaces: Mammoth Tank",
	"Actor-apoc.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increased firepower\n+ Increased health\n+ Increased range\n+ Increased splash damage",
	"Actor-armor.doctrine-Description2": "Specialize in tanks:\n• Rhino Tank (replaces Heavy Tank)\n• Apocalypse Tank (replaces Mammoth Tank)\n• Reactive Armor Upgrade\n• Tank Drop\n• Industrial Plant\n\n",
	"Actor-arty.doctrine-Description2": "Specialize in artillery:\n• Grad (replaces Katyusha)\n• Nuke Cannon\n• Rocket Pods Upgrade\n• Kill Zone\n• Munitions Plant\n\n",
	"Actor-atomicengines.upgrade-Description2": "Upgrades tanks with volatile atomic engines.\n\nReplaces: Heavy/Lasher Tank\nReplaces: Rhino/Thrasher Tank\nReplaces: Eradicator\nReplaces: Mammoth Tank\nReplaces: Overlord Tank\nReplaces: Apocalypse Tank",
	"Actor-avenger.upgrade-Description2": "Replaces Warthog's incendiary bombs with GAU-8 Avenger rotary cannon and Hydra rockets.\n\nUpgrades: Warthog",
	"Actor-avenger.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increased damage\n+ Increased range",
	"Actor-bdrone.upgrade-Description2": "Allows construction of remotely piloted Battle Tanks.\n\nReplaces: Battle Tank",
	"Actor-bdrone.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Reduced cost\n+ Increased rate of fire\n+ Self-repair\n• XP of losses reclaimed by replacements\n+ Immunity to crew kill, chaos gas and mind control",
	"Actor-bdrone.upgrade-Weaknesses2": "– Reduced HP\n– Reduced damage\n– Disabled if radar is down\n– Can be hacked",
	"Actor-bjet.upgrade-Weaknesses2": "– Weak vs Heavy Armor\n– Has difficulty hitting moving targets\n– Cannot attack Aircraft",
	"Actor-blacknapalm.upgrade-Description2": "Superheated flame weapons that can melt armored targets.\n\nUpgrades: Heavy Flame Tank\nUpgrades: SSM Launcher\nUpgrades: Avatar",
	"Actor-blink.upgrade-Description2": "Equips Intruders and Watchers with blink packs allowing them to teleport.\n\nUpgrades: Intruder\nUpgrades: Marauder\nUpgrades: Watcher",
	"Actor-bombard.strat-Attributes2": "\n(!) Only ONE Strategy may be chosen.",
	"Actor-bombard.strat-Description2": "Firepower focused strategy, required for:\n• Zone Trooper\n• Tomahawk Launcher Research\n• Hailstorm Missiles Upgrade\n• Avenger Upgrade\n• Firestorm Missiles Power\n\n",
	"Actor-bombard3.strat-Strengths2": "+ Increases firepower and rate of fire of vehicles and aircraft by a further 3%\n+ Unlocks Firestorm Missile Barrage power",
	"Actor-carapace.upgrade-Description2": "Infantry gain a hardened carapace which provides protection against explosives.\n\nUpgrades: Infantry",
	"Actor-ceramic.upgrade-Description2": "Upgrades Warthogs with ceramic armor.\n\nUpgrades: Warthog",
	"Actor-charv.upgrade-Description2": "Allows construction of Chrono Miners which\nteleport back to refineries.\n\nUpgrades: Ore Truck",
	"Actor-coalescence.upgrade-Description2": "On death or when deployed, Leechers will transform into a ball of bio-matter which heals nearby allies and eventually coalesces into a new Leecher.\n\nUpgrades: Leecher",
	"Actor-coalescence.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Leecher able to resurrect\n+ Heals allies while in coalescence form",
	"Actor-covenant.upgrade-Description2": "Upgrade depends on chosen covenant.\n\n• Wrath: Laser Tanks\n• Unity: Custodian\n• Zeal: Raider Buggy",
	"Actor-covenant.upgrade2-Description2": "Upgrade depends on chosen covenant.\n\n• Wrath: Cyborg Firepower\n• Unity: Augmented Fabrication\n• Zeal: Cyborg Speed",
	"Actor-cryw.upgrade-Description2": "Arms certain rocket equipped units with Cryo warheads which cause targets to move more slowly and take increased damage.\n\nUpgrades: Rocket Soldier\nUpgrades: Longbow\nUpgrades: Guardian GI (USA only)\nUpgrades: Nighthawk (USA only)",
	"Actor-cust.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Heavy armor\n+ Heals cyborgs & repairs vehicles",
	"Actor-cust.upgrade-Weaknesses2": "– No stealth capability\n– No offensive capability\n– Reduced speed\n– Increased cost",
	"Actor-cyborgarmor.upgrade-Description2": "Improves cyborg armor.\n\nUpgrades: Cyborg\nUpgrades: Cyborg Rocket Soldier\nUpgrades: Chemical Warrior\nUpgrades: Acolyte/Templar\nUpgrades: Cyborg Mechanic\nUpgrades: Cyberscrin/Cyberdog\nUpgrades: Enlightened\nUpgrades: Cyborg Reaper\nUpgrades: Cyborg Elite",
	"Actor-cyborgarmor.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ 20% reduced damage taken\n+ Additional 10% reduced damage from explosives",
	"Actor-cyborgdmg.upgrade-Description2": "Increases cyborg firepower.\n\nUpgrades: Cyborg\nUpgrades: Cyborg Rocket Soldier\nUpgrades: Chemical Warrior\nUpgrades: Acolyte/Templar\nUpgrades: Cyborg Mechanic\nUpgrades: Cyberscrin/Cyberdog\nUpgrades: Cyborg Elite",
	"Actor-cyborgspeed.upgrade-Description2": "Increases cyborg movement speed.\n\nUpgrades: Cyborg\nUpgrades: Cyborg Rocket Soldier\nUpgrades: Chemical Warrior\nUpgrades: Acolyte/Templar\nUpgrades: Cyborg Mechanic\nUpgrades: Cyberscrin/Cyberdog\nUpgrades: Enlightened\nUpgrades: Cyborg Elite",
	"Actor-decoy.upgrade-Description2": "Grant Buggies the ability to project a pair of decoy Flame Tanks. Decoys provide small area of vision for a short time after being killed.\n\nUpgrades: Buggy\nUpgrades: Raider Buggy",
	"Actor-defense.policy-Attributes2": "(!) Only ONE Policy may be chosen.\n(!) HP bonuses do not stack",
	"Actor-defense.policy-Description2": "Pursue defense policy.\n\n• Level 1: +15% building/defense HP, +25% Construction Yard build radius\n• Level 2: +30% building/defense HP, +40% building repair rate, +50% building vision radius\n• Level 3: +25% defense vision radius, +20% defense repair rate, +15% defense weapon damage, +2 gap generator shroud radius",
	"Actor-delp.upgrade-Description": "Allows construction of the Delphis APC.\n\nReplaces: APC",
	"Actor-delp.upgrade-Name": "Research: Delphis APC",
	"Actor-delp.upgrade-Strengths": "+ Turreted sonic weapon that weakens structures",
	"Actor-delp.upgrade-Weaknesses": "– Increased cost\n– Decreased unit speed",
	"Actor-deso.upgrade-Description2": "Rad Troopers are phased out in favor of Desolators.\n\nReplaces: Rad Trooper",
	"Actor-deso.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increased health\n+ Increased damage\n+ Irradiates vehicles\n+ Desolate Ground ability",
	"Actor-development.policy-Attributes2": "(!) Only ONE Policy may be chosen.(!) XP bonuses do not stack",
	"Actor-development.policy-Description2": "Pursue development policy.\n\n• Level 1: +20% unit experience gain\n• Level 2: +40% unit experience gain, 15% discount on Tech Center, HQ & all upgrades\n• Level 3: +60% unit experience gain, rank 3 units gain additional health & damage",
	"Actor-doctrine.upgrade1-Description2": "Upgrade depends on chosen doctrine.\n\n• Infantry: Improved Paratroopers\n• Tanks: Reactive Armor\n• Artillery: Rocket Pods",
	"Actor-doctrine.upgrade2-Description2": "Upgrade depends on chosen doctrine.\n\n• Infantry: Overlord Tank\n• Tanks: Apocalypse Tank\n• Artillery: Nuke Cannon",
	"Actor-economy.policy-Attributes2": "(!) Only ONE Policy may be chosen.(!) Cost reductions do not stack",
	"Actor-economy.policy-Description2": "Pursue economic policy.\n\n• Level 1: -15% cost of Refineries, Harvesters & MCVs\n• Level 2: -20% cost of Refineries, Harvesters & MCVs, +20% MCV movement speed\n• Level 3: -25% cost of Refineries, Harvesters & MCVs, Free Chrono Miner upgrade, +50% Ore Purifier income",
	"Actor-ejjet.upgrade-Description": "Improves the speed and vision of Jumpjet Troopers and Bombardiers and grants them cloak detection.\n\nUpgrades: Jumpjet Infantry\nUpgrades: Bombardier",
	"Actor-ejjet.upgrade-Name": "Upgrade: Enhanced Jumpjets",
	"Actor-ejjet.upgrade-Strengths": "+ 25% faster movement\n+ Vision range increased by 2\n+ Cloak detection",
	"Actor-empgren.upgrade-Description2": "Upgrades Grenadier to use EMP Grenades.\n\nUpgrades: Grenadier",
	"Actor-empgren.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Grenades briefly disable vehicles and defenses\n+ Grenadiers no longer explode when killed",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.buffs.frenzy-Strengths2": "+33% rate of fire\n+25% movement speed",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.buffs.frenzy-Weaknesses2": "-15% rate of fire after effect ends\n-15% movement speed after effect ends",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.buffs.hotu-Strengths2": "Effective health boosted to 28k\n+20% movement speed\n+50% range\n+50% rate of fire",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.buffs.inspiration-Strengths2": "+15% movement speed\n+10% rate of fire",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.buffs.inspiration2-Strengths2": "+30% movement speed\n+20% rate of fire",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.buffs.ironcurtain-EncyclopediaExtras-Description": "Soviet minor superweapon effect which grants temporary invulnerability (still affected by debuffs).",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.buffs.tibstealth-Strengths2": "• Invisible to enemies\n-10% damage taken",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.debuffs.atomized-Weaknesses2": "• Deals periodic damage\n-33% movement speed\n-33% damage dealt",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.debuffs.berserk-Attributes2": "+25% movement speed\n+100% rate of fire",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.debuffs.blinded-Weaknesses2": "• Vision disabled\n• Weapons disabled",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.debuffs.chill-Weaknesses2": "-25/35/43/50/56/59/62/65/68/70% movement speed\n+10% damage received per stack",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.debuffs.concussion-Weaknesses2": "-25% movement speed\n-50% rate of fire",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.debuffs.emp-Weaknesses2": "• Movement disabled\n• Weapons disabled\n• Abilities disabled\n• Unshielded aircraft crash to ground",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.debuffs.irradiated-Weaknesses2": "• Deals periodic damage to nearby units\n• Irradiates the ground\n-10% damage dealt\n+10% damage received",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.debuffs.jammed-EncyclopediaExtras-Description": "Applied by Allied Radar Jammers. Reduces vehicle and aircraft weapon damage and rate of fire.",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.debuffs.jammed-Weaknesses2": "-10% damage dealt\n-20% rate of fire",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.debuffs.reapersnared-Weaknesses2": "• Movement disabled\n• Weapons disabled\n• Abilities disabled",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.debuffs.suppression-Weaknesses2": "-60% movement speed\n-20% rate of fire",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.debuffs.targetpainted-Weaknesses2": "Revealed to enemies\n+10% damage received",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.debuffs.underminedfoundation-EncyclopediaExtras-Description": "Applied by the Allied Delphis APC. Buildings take greatly increased damage.",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.debuffs.underminedfoundation-Name": "Undermined Foundation",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.debuffs.underminedfoundation-Weaknesses": "+60% damage received",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.debuffs.veiled-Weaknesses2": "-20% weapon range\n-20% vision range",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.ifv.conf-Attributes2": "• Explosion causes units to attack indiscriminately\n• Passenger: Confessor",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.ifv.cryo-Attributes2": "• Slows enemy units and makes them take increased damage\n• Passenger: Cryo Trooper",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.ifv.cryo-Weaknesses2": "• Weak vs Buildings, Defenses\n• Cannot attack Aircraft",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.ifv.engi-Attributes2": "• Captures structures\n• Passenger: Engineer",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.ifv.hack-Weaknesses2": "• Cannot deal damage\n• Control lost if passenger exits",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.ifv.hopl-Weaknesses2": "• Weak vs Heavy Armor\n• Cannot attack Aircraft",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.ifv.mech-Attributes2": "• Repairs friendly vehicles\n• Passenger: Mechanic",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.ifv.med-Attributes2": "• Heals friendly infantry\n• Passenger: Medic",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.ifv.mortchem-Weaknesses2": "• Weak vs Heavy Armor\n• Cannot attack Aircraft\n• Has difficulty hitting moving targets",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.ifv.psy-Attributes2": "• Can mind control enemy units\n• Control lost if passenger exits\n• Passenger: Yuri, Mastermind",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.ifv.psy-Weaknesses2": "• Cannot deal damage\n• Cannot attack Aircraft",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.ifv.snip-Weaknesses2": "• Weak vs Defenses, Buildings\n• Cannot attack Aircraft",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.ifv.spy-Attributes2": "• Targets are reaveled and take increased damage",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.ifv.spy-EncyclopediaExtras-Description": "IFV loaded with a Spy. Paints targets to reveal them and make them take increased damage.",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.power.assassinsquad-EncyclopediaExtras-Description": "Deploy a squad of Assassins that can snipe infantry from long range and destroy buildings with C4.\n\nTarget infantry production structure to deploy.",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.power.atomicammo-EncyclopediaExtras-Description": "Grants tanks a limited supply of atomic shells (also for a limited duration).\n\nAffects Soviet tanks only (Heavy/Rhino Tank, Lasher/Thrasher Tank, Siege Tank, Mammoth Tank, Overlord Tank, Apocalypse Tank, Nuke Cannon)",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.power.chemmissile-EncyclopediaExtras-Description": "Launches an deadly Chemical Missile. Deals heavy damage and creates toxic clouds which are extremely harmful to infantry.\n",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.power.chronoshift-EncyclopediaExtras-Description": "Teleports up to 9 selected vehicles to a targeted location, returning them to their original location after a short time.\n\n• If killed, units are returned with 20% health\n• Units with larger health pools take additional damage\n• Passengers cannot be unloaded\n• Enemy units are teleported for reduced duration",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.power.colonyspike-EncyclopediaExtras-Description": "Creates a Colony Spike at the target location. Enables production of non-defensive structures.\n\nWhen fully charged allows non-defensive structures to be built nearby.\n\nMust be built within range of a Colony Platform.",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.power.confessorcabal-EncyclopediaExtras-Description": "Deploy a Confessor Cabal which is able to construct Idols of Kane that buffs allies and debuffs enemies.\n\nTarget infantry production structure to deploy.",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.power.fleetrecall-EncyclopediaExtras-Description": "Recalls all selected Scrin fleet vessels back to the Signal Transmitter.\n\nApplies to: Mothership, Planetary Assault Carrier, Devastator",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.power.forceshield-EncyclopediaExtras-Description": "Makes selected friendly structures temporarily invulnerable.\n\nWarning: Causes power failure.",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.power.frenzy-EncyclopediaExtras-Description": "Increases the movement speed and rate of fire of targeted units for a limited time.\n\nWarning: Units are weakened for a short time after frenzy wears off.",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.power.gateway-EncyclopediaExtras-Description": "Creates a Gateway at the target location. Acts as the exit for any\n   targeted infantry or vehicle production structure.\n\nRequires target location to be within vision.",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.power.greatercoalescence-EncyclopediaExtras-Description": "Spawns a controllable biomass which heals nearby allies and sustains itself by feeding off enemies.\n\nFeeding from power plants will shut them down temporarily.",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.power.hackercell-EncyclopediaExtras-Description": "Deploy a squad of Hackers that can remotely capture buildings and take control of defenses.\n\nTarget infantry production structure to deploy.",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.power.heroes-EncyclopediaExtras-Description": "Targeted basic infantry units become Heroes of the Union, significantly increasing their damage, speed, range and resilience.\n\nCan affect Rifle Infantry, Rocket Soldiers, Grenadiers and Flamethrowers.",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.power.ichorspike-EncyclopediaExtras-Description": "Creates an Ichor Spike at the target location. Resources within its area of influence grow and spread faster.\n\nAlso empowers units with Resource Conversion upgrade.",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.power.recondrone-EncyclopediaExtras-Description": "A drone flies across the map, revealing the area as it passes.\n\nDetects cloaked units.",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.power.shadowteam-EncyclopediaExtras-Description": "Calls for a Shadow Team; three stealth infantry that arrive via glider armed with grenades and a machine pistol.\n\nOperatives can be ordered to land via the deploy command.",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.power.techhack-EncyclopediaExtras-Description": "Hack the targeted enemy production structure, providing access to a unit developed using enemy technology.\n\nFor infantry, vehicle and air production respectively: \n\n• Allies: Cryo Mortar, Reckoner, Phantom\n• Soviets: Cyberdog, Cyclops, Kamov\n• GDI: Sonic Mortar, Basilisk, Shade\n• Nod: Chem Mortar, Mantis, Vertigo\n• Scrin: Cyberscrin, Viper, Manticore",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.power.tibstealth-EncyclopediaExtras-Description": "Makes selected vehicles and structures temporarily invisible.\n\nWarning: Harmful to non-cyborg infantry.\n\nHazmat Suits upgrade makes allies immune to damage and enemies take 50% damage.",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.power.voidspike-EncyclopediaExtras-Description": "Creates a Voidspike at the target location. Gradually transforms nearby resources into Black Tiberium which is devoid of most of its useful properties.\n\nDamages nearby enemy units.",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.reck.spy-Attributes2": "• Sabotages enemy structures:\n    • Power Plants: Power outage\n    • Barracks/Factory: Infantry/vehicles produced as veteran\n    • Superweapons: Reset timer\n    • Radar: Reset shroud\n    • Helipad: Single-use paratroopers\n    • Airfield/Gravity Stabilizer: Single-use airstrike\n• Passenger: Spy",
	"Actor-encyclopedia.tips.general-EncyclopediaExtras-Description": "• Most infantry prone when they are fired upon, which makes them move more slowly but makes them take 50% less damage.\n• Primary anti-aircraft vehicles (IFV, BTR, Vulcan, Stealth Tank and Gun/Shard Walker) and static anti-aircraft defenses take 50% damage from aircraft.\n• Primary anti-aircraft units and aircraft with air-to-air capability will prioritize firing at aircraft when auto targeting or attack moving.\n• Most anti-air weapons will deal splash damage in a large radius. This is to increase the diminishing returns of massing aircraft.\n• When low power all production is reduced to half speed.\n• Units will only move to attack in Attack Anything stance.\n• Cloaked units can be detected by any adjacent infantry, as well as by scout units and certain other detectors.\n• Helipads/Airfields will repair landed aircraft if they are close to a Service Depot (or its equivalents).\n• Many units have abilities that can be used via the deploy key (F by default).\n• You can control the direction of most reinforcement/airstrike support powers by dragging the mouse.\n• The \"Competitive\" production type is designed to reduce the effectiveness of tier 1 spam. Each production structure has its own queue, but additional production structures of each type initially cost significantly more than the first, and the cost can then be reduced by building a Radar or Service Depot, and further reduced by building a Tech Center or Allied HQ.\n• Transports can be mass loaded using Alt-click. It will cause all selected units to fill the closest transports of the type that was clicked on.\n• Upgrades with an yellow-orange border are sidegrades, meaning they have negative as well as positive effects.\n• Upgrades with a \"beaker\" icon in the top right do not affect existing units, which either need to be upgraded via a Service Depot (or equivalent), or cannot be upgraded.\n• Mines and explosives attached to buildings (C4, TNT) can be disarmed by Engineers/Assimilators.\n• Bridges can be repaired by Engineers/Assimilators (they are not consumed in the process).\n• Structures that provide support powers, advanced defences, and the Radar Dome (or its equivalents) can be powered down using the power down key (X by default) or using the button in the top right.\n• Neutral structures can be captured by Engineers/Assumilators even after they have been destroyed.\n• Service Depot repairs are completely free. Vehicles can be sold while being repaired.\n• All production times are proportional to cost. The cost to time ratio is lower for Refineries, MCVs and higher for upgrades.\n• In Single Queue the maximum production speed is 2x, which requires 5 infantry/aircraft production structures, or 4 vehicle/building production structures.",
	"Actor-entrench.upgrade-Description2": "Enables Engineers to facilitate the building of defenses.\n\nUpgrades: Engineer",
	"Actor-erad.upgrade-Description2": "Upgrades Mammoth tanks with volatile radiation cannon.\n\nReplaces: Mammoth Tank",
	"Actor-erad.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ High area damage vs infantry and vehicles\n+ Irradiates impacted vehicles\n+ Increased range",
	"Actor-erad.upgrade-Weaknesses2": "– Loses AA missiles\n– Reduced single-target anti-tank damage\n– Reduced damage vs buildings",
	"Actor-evis.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increased damage\n+ Increased health\n+ Increased rate of fire\n+ Benefits from Resource Conversion upgrade",
	"Actor-evis.upgrade-Weaknesses2": "– Increased cost\n– Reduced range",
	"Actor-flakarmor.upgrade-Description2": "Infantry are equipped with advanced flak armor which provides protection against explosives.\n\nUpgrades: Infantry",
	"Actor-flakarmor.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ 40% reduced damage from explosives\n+ 20% reduced damage from incendiary explosives",
	"Actor-gattling.upgrade-Description2": "Upgrades BTRs with dual gattling cannons.\n\nReplaces: BTR",
	"Actor-greece.coalition-Description2": "Form a coalition with Greece, required for:\n• Hoplite\n• Zeus Artillery\n• Helios Bomb",
	"Actor-gyro.upgrade-Description2": "Allows mech units to activate gyro stabilizers, increasing range but reducing rate of fire.\n\nUpgrades: Wolverine\nUpgrades: Titan\nUpgrades: Railgun Titan\nUpgrades: Juggernaut",
	"Actor-gyro.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Added Gyro Stabilizers ability (increased range, reduced rate of fire)\n+ Increases Juggernaut range by 50%.",
	"Actor-hailstorm.upgrade-Description2": "Equip the MLRS/HMLRS with Hailstorm Missiles.\n\nUpgrades: MLRS/HMLRS",
	"Actor-hailstorm.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increased damage and area of effect\n+ Fires six missiles per salvo",
	"Actor-hammerhead.upgrade-Description2": "Equip the MLRS/HMLRS with Hammerhead Missiles.\n\nUpgrades: MLRS/HMLRS",
	"Actor-hammerhead.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increased damage and area of effect\n+ Briefly slows movement and rate of fire of impacted targets",
	"Actor-hazmat.upgrade-Description2": "Infantry are equipped with hazmat suits which provides protection against Tiberium and radiation.\n\nUpgrades: Infantry",
	"Actor-hazmat.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Tiberium immunity\n+ 50% resistance to irradiated terrain",
	"Actor-hazmatsoviet.upgrade-Description2": "Infantry are equipped with heavy hazmat suits which provides protection against Tiberium and radiation.\n\nUpgrades: Infantry",
	"Actor-hazmatsoviet.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Tiberium immunity\n+ High resistance to irradiated terrain",
	"Actor-hold.strat-Description2": "Defensive strategy, required for:\n• Zone Defender\n• Point Defense Systems Upgrade\n• Hammerhead Missiles Upgrade\n• Ceramic Armor Upgrade\n• Nanite Shield Power\n\n",
	"Actor-hold3.strat-Strengths2": "+ Increases armor of vehicles and aircraft by a further 5%\n+ Unlocks Nanite Shield power",
	"Actor-hovermam.upgrade-Description2": "Allows construction of the Hover Mammoth Tank.\n\nReplaces: Mammoth Tank",
	"Actor-hovermam.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Faster movement speed\n+ Can traverse water",
	"Actor-howi.upgrade-Description2": "Allows construction of Howitzers.\n\nReplaces: Artillery",
	"Actor-howi.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increased projectile speed\n+ Increased movement speed\n+ Increased accuracy\n+ Increased burst damage\n+ Increased vision\n+ Has turret",
	"Actor-howi.upgrade-Weaknesses2": "– Reduced splash radius\n– Reduced range\n– Reduced rate of fire",
	"Actor-hstk.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increased damage\n+ Increased durability",
	"Actor-hstk.upgrade-Weaknesses2": "– Reduced mobility\n– Increased cost\n– Increased cloaking delay",
	"Actor-hyper.upgrade-Description2": "Seekers and Lacerators gain Hypercharge ability, allow them to fire an uninterrupted barrage for a limited time. Increased damage taken while active. After use, weapon damage and speed is reduced for a short time.\n\nUpgrades: Seeker\nUpgrades: Lacerator",
	"Actor-hypersonic.upgrade-Description2": "Equip the MLRS/HMLRS with Hypersonic Missiles.\n\nUpgrades: MLRS/HMLRS",
	"Actor-impl.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increased range\n+ Increased damage\n+ Increased health\n+ Slows targets",
	"Actor-impl.upgrade-Weaknesses2": "– Increased cost\n– Reduced speed\n– Reduced rate of fire",
	"Actor-impmuta.upgrade-Description2": "Enhances Genetic Mutation Bomb and Brutes.\n\nUpgrades: Genetic Mutation Bomb\nUpgrades: Brute",
	"Actor-impmuta.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increased area of effect (Mutation Bomb)\n+ Increased maximum number of targets (Mutation Bomb)\n+ Increased movement speed (Brute)",
	"Actor-imppara.upgrade-Description2": "Upgrades the Paratroopers support power.\n\nUpgrades: Paratroopers",
	"Actor-impstorm.upgrade-Description2": "Upgrades the Stormtroopers support power.\n\nUpgrades: Stormtroopers",
	"Actor-infantry.doctrine-Description2": "Specialize in infantry:\n• Troop Crawler\n• Overlord Tank (replaces Mammoth Tank)\n• Improved Paratroopers Upgrade\n• Heroes of the Union\n• Cloning Vat\n\n",
	"Actor-influence.level1-Description2": "Influence Level 1",
	"Actor-influence.level2-Description2": "Influence Level 2",
	"Actor-influence.level3-Description2": "Influence Level 3",
	"Actor-ioncon.upgrade-Description2": "Allows Storm Columns, Storm Spikes and Stormcrawlers to store ion energy and release it into the atmosphere, creating a localized Ion Storm.\n\nUpgrades: Storm Column\nUpgrades: Stormcrawler\nUpgrades: Storm Spike",
	"Actor-ioncon.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increases damage and range over time when active\n+ Reduces incoming damage over time when active\n+ Ion storm can damage enemy units and structures",
	"Actor-ionmam.upgrade-Description2": "Allows construction of the Ion Mammoth Tank.\n\nReplaces: Mammoth Tank",
	"Actor-ionmam.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increased range\n+ Increased area of effect",
	"Actor-korea.coalition-Description2": "Form a coalition with South Korea, required for:\n• Tiger Guard\n• Black Eagle\n• Black Sky Strike",
	"Actor-lasher.upgrade-Description2": "Upgrades Heavy/Rhino tanks with infantry crushing attachment at the cost of some armor and firepower.\n\nReplaces: Heavy Tank\nReplaces: Rhino Tank",
	"Actor-lasher.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ 25% faster movement\n+ Improved crushing performance",
	"Actor-lasher.upgrade-Weaknesses2": "– Reduced hit points\n– Reduced firepower",
	"Actor-lastnk.upgrade-Description2": "Upgrades: Light Tank\nUpgrades: Battle Tank",
	"Actor-lastnk.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increased damage vs infantry & light armor\n+ Increased range",
	"Actor-loyalist.allegiance-Description2": "Declare your allegiance and side with the Scrin Overlord.\n\nRequired for:\n• Eviscerator\n• Ruiner\n• Overlord's Wrath\n• Ichor Spike\n\n",
	"Actor-malefic.allegiance-Description2": "Declare your allegiance and side with the Malefic Scrin.\n\nRequired for:\n• Stalker\n• Darkener\n• Anathema\n• Voidspike\n\n",
	"Actor-mdrone.upgrade-Description2": "Allows construction of remotely piloted Mammoth Tanks.\n\nReplaces: Mammoth Tank",
	"Actor-mdrone.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Reduced cost\n+ Increased rate of fire\n+ Improved self-repair\n• XP of losses reclaimed by replacements\n+ Immunity to crew kill, chaos gas and mind control",
	"Actor-microwave.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Kills crew of vehicles with less than 75% HP\n + Increased EMP duration for direct target\n+ EMP affects adjacent vehicles/defenses",
	"Actor-mpspawn-Name": "(multiplayer player starting point)",
	"Actor-nukc.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Strong vs Buildings, Defenses, Infantry, Light Armor\n+ Extremely long range",
	"Actor-nukc.upgrade-Weaknesses2": "– Must deploy to fire\n– Slow rate of fire\n– Slow projectiles",
	"Actor-optics.upgrade-Description2": "Equips rangers with advanced optics which temporarily extends their vision and detection range.\n\nUpgrades: Ranger",
	"Actor-ovld.upgrade-Description2": "Allows production of Overlord Tanks.\n\nReplaces: Mammoth Tank",
	"Actor-ovld.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increased health\n+ Increased firepower\n+ Increased range\n+ Empowers nearby infantry",
	"Actor-ovld.upgrade-Weaknesses2": "– Reduced speed\n– Increased cost",
	"Actor-pcan.upgrade-Description2": "Allows construction of Prism Cannons.\n\nReplaces: Prism Tank",
	"Actor-pcan.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increased range\n+ Increased burst damage",
	"Actor-pcan.upgrade-Weaknesses2": "– Reduced rate of fire\n– Reduced mobility",
	"Actor-playerxp.level1-Name2": "Player Rank 1",
	"Actor-playerxp.level2-Name2": "Player Rank 2",
	"Actor-playerxp.level3-Name2": "Player Rank 3",
	"Actor-pointdef.upgrade-Description2": "Equips several units with point defense shields and/or point defense lasers which protect against enemy fire.\n\nUpgrades: Battle Tank (Shield and Laser)\nUpgrades: Battle Drone (Shield and Laser)\nUpgrades: Harvester (Shield)\nUpgrades: Frigate (Laser)",
	"Actor-pointdef.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Added Point Defense Shield\n+ Added Point Defense Laser",
	"Actor-powerproxy.airborne-Name2": "Airdrop: Guardian GIs",
	"Actor-powerproxy.airborne.tank-Name2": "Airdrop: Grizzly Tanks",
	"Actor-powerproxy.paratroopers-Description": "A Halo transport drops a squad of infantry\nanywhere on the map.",
	"Actor-powerproxy.paratroopers-Name": "Paratroopers (Single Use)",
	"Actor-powerproxy.paratroopers.allies-Description": "A Chinook drops a squad of infantry\nanywhere on the map.",
	"Actor-powerproxy.sonarpulse-Description": "Reveals all submarines in the vicinity for a \nshort time.",
	"Actor-powerproxy.sonarpulse-Name": "Sonar Pulse",
	"Actor-quantum.upgrade-Description2": "Enhances heavy laser weapons.\n\nUpgrades: Obelisk of Light\nUpgrades: Avatar\nUpgrades: Laser Turret\nUpgrades: Venom\nUpgrades: Templar",
	"Actor-quantum.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increased range\n+ Increased damage",
	"Actor-railgun.upgrade-Description2": "Allows construction of the Railgun Titan.\n\nReplaces: Titan",
	"Actor-railgun.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increased range\n+ Damages targets in a line",
	"Actor-rbug.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Heavy armor\n+ Increased damage\n+ Increased range",
	"Actor-reactive.upgrade-Description2": "Upgrades Rhino Tanks and BTRs with reactive armor for additional protection.\n\nUpgrades: Rhino Tank\nUpgrades: Thrasher Tank\nUpgrades: BTR\nUpgrades: Gattling BTR",
	"Actor-rebel.allegiance-Description2": "Declare your allegiance and side with the Scrin Rebels.\n\nRequired for:\n• Impaler\n• Nullifier\n• Gateway\n• Colony Spike\n\n",
	"Actor-regen.upgrade-Description2": "Scrin aircraft and Stormcrawlers will regenerate health over time when not in combat.\n\nUpgrades: Stormrider\nUpgrades: Tormentor\nUpgrades: Enervator\nUpgrades: Devastator Warship\nUpgrades: Planetary Assault Carrier\nUpgrades: Mothership\nUpgrades: Stormcrawler",
	"Actor-resconv.upgrade-Description2": "Weapons of certain units are empowered by Tiberium and other resources. Reaper Tripod gains additional charges.\n\nUpgrades: Devourer\nUpgrades: Ruiner\nUpgrades: Reaper Tripod\nUpgrades: Eviscerator\nUpgrades: Corrupter (Reaper-17 only)",
	"Actor-resconv.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increased damage when charged\n+ Doubled charge capacity (Reaper Tripod only)",
	"Actor-rocketpods.upgrade-Description2": "Upgrades Grad and Hind rocket pods.\n\nUpgrades: Grad\nUpgrades: Hind",
	"Actor-rocketpods.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increased salvo size (Grad)\n+ Increased ammo & rate of fire (Hind)",
	"Actor-seek.strat-Description2": "Speed and weapon range focused strategy, required for:\n• Zone Raider\n• Enhanced Jumpjets Upgrade\n• Hypersonic Missiles Upgrade\n• Sidewinders Upgrade\n• Advanced Radar Power\n\n",
	"Actor-seek3.strat-Strengths2": "+ Increases speed and weapon range of vehicles and aircraft by a further 5%\n+ Unlocks Advanced Radar Scan power",
	"Actor-seismic.upgrade-Description2": "Arms the Sukhoi with Seismic Missiles.\n\nUpgrades: Sukhoi",
	"Actor-seismic.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ High area damage vs structures and vehicles\n+ Slows movement and rate of fire of impacted targets",
	"Actor-sharv.upgrade-Description2": "Allows construction of Stealth Harvesters which are cloaked while moving.\n\nUpgrades: Harvester",
	"Actor-shields.upgrade-Description2": "Equip Scrin airborne units and certain ground units with shields.\n\nUpgrades: Interloper\nUpgrades: Stormcrawler\nUpgrades: Stormrider\nUpgrades: Tormentor\nUpgrades: Enervator\nUpgrades: Devastator Warship\nUpgrades: Planetary Assault Carrier\nUpgrades: Mothership",
	"Actor-shields.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Grants an additonal health pool\n+ Resistance to EMP for aircraft",
	"Actor-shrw.upgrade-Description2": "Allows production of Shard Walkers, a heavier and more powerful variant of the Gun Walker.\n\nReplaces: Gun Walker",
	"Actor-shrw.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increased durability\n+ Increased damage",
	"Actor-shrw.upgrade-Weaknesses2": "– Slower movement\n– Slower projectiles",
	"Actor-sidewinders.upgrade-Description2": "Equips Warthogs with air-to-air missiles.\n\nUpgrades: Warthog",
	"Actor-sonic.upgrade-Description2": "Improve the weapons of Disruptors and Sonic Towers.\n\nUpgrades: Sonic Tower\nUpgrades: Disruptor",
	"Actor-sonic.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increased damage\n+ Increased range\n+ Slows enemy movement and rate of fire",
	"Actor-stellar.upgrade-Description2": "Devastator Warships upgraded with stellar fusion cannon.\n\nUpgrades: Devastator Warship",
	"Actor-stellar.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increased damage\n+ Increased area of effect\n+ Improved accuracy\n+ Faster projectile",
	"Actor-stlk.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increased damage\n+ Increased health\n+ Cloaking ability with speed boost",
	"Actor-stlk.upgrade-Weaknesses2": "– Increased cost\n– Reduced splash damage",
	"Actor-strata10.upgrade-Description2": "Upgrade depends on chosen strategy.\n\n• Bombardment: Avenger upgrade\n• Seek & Destroy: Sidewinders upgrade\n• Hold the Line: Ceramic Armor upgrade",
	"Actor-strategic.upgrade-Description2": "Upgrade depends on chosen strategy.\n\n• Bombardment: Tomahawk Launcher research\n• Seek & Destroy: Enhanced Jumpjets upgrade\n• Hold the Line: Point Defense Systems upgrade",
	"Actor-stratmiss.upgrade-Description2": "Equip the MLRS/HMLRS with improved missiles depending on chosen strategy.\n\n• Bombardment: Hailstorm Missiles\n• Seek & Destroy: Hypersonic Missiles\n• Hold the Line: Hammerhead Missiles",
	"Actor-sweden.coalition-Description2": "Form a coalition with Sweden, required for:\n• Cryo Trooper\n• Cryo Launcher\n• Cryostorm",
	"Actor-tarc.upgrade-Description2": "Upgrades the Tesla Tank and Tesla Track weapon.\n\nUpgrades: Tesla Tank\nUpgrades: Tesla Track",
	"Actor-tdog.upgrade-Description2": "Attack Dogs are strapped with explosives.\n\nReplaces: Attack Dog",
	"Actor-tdog.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Able to damage vehicles and buildings\n+ Trained to detect scent of enemy vehicles",
	"Actor-tdog.upgrade-Weaknesses2": "– Explodes on attack or on death\n– No longer detects scent of enemy infantry\n– Reduced detection range\n– Increased cost",
	"Actor-tflx.upgrade-Description2": "Units gain increased movement speed and rate of fire after being chronoshifted.\n\nUpgrades: Chronoshift\n\nUpgrades: Chrono Prison\nUpgrades: Chrono Tank",
	"Actor-tflx.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ 33% increased movement & rate of fire for 8s after chronoshifting",
	"Actor-thwk.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Strong vs Buildings\n+ Extremely long range",
	"Actor-thwk.upgrade-Weaknesses2": "– Projectiles can be shot down\n– Slow rate of fire",
	"Actor-tibcore.upgrade-Description2": "Upgrade to Tiberium Core missiles.\n\nUpgrades: Recon Bike\nUpgrades: Stealth Tank\nUpgrades: Cyborg Rocket Soldier\nUpgrades: Rocket Soldier",
	"Actor-tibcore.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increased range\n+ Increased damage\n+ Increased projectile speed",
	"Actor-tow.upgrade-Description2": "Hum-Vees and Guardian Drones will be produced with TOW missile launchers.\n\nReplaces: Hum-Vee\nReplaces: Guardian Drone",
	"Actor-ttrp.upgrade-Description2": "Shock Troopers are phased out in favor of Tesla Troopers.\n\nReplaces: Shock Trooper",
	"Actor-ttrp.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Increased health\n+ Increased rate of fire\n+ Increased damage",
	"Actor-unity.covenant-Description2": "Adopt the Covenant of Unity.\n\n• Level 1: Hacker Squad, Internet Center & Siphoned Funds ($ from Hackers in Internet Center)\n• Level 2: Cyborg Armor & Custodian Upgrades\n• Level 3: Cyborg Reaper, Cyborg Elite & Reclaimed Fabrication Upgrade",
	"Actor-vulcan.upgrade-Strengths2": "+ Adds anti-air capability\n+ Increased damage against ground targets\n+ Adds turret",
	"Actor-vulcan.upgrade-Weaknesses2": "– Increased cost\n– Reduced speed",
	"Actor-waypoint-Name": "(waypoint for scripted behavior)",
	"Actor-wrath.covenant-Description2": "Adopt the Covenant of Wrath.\n\n• Level 1: Assassin Squad & Compressed Plasma (+3 Banshee ammo)\n• Level 2: Cyborg Armor & Laser Tanks Upgrades\n• Level 3: Avatar, Cyborg Elite & Cyborg Firepower Upgrade",
	"Actor-zeal.covenant-Description2": "Adopt the Covenant of Zeal.\n\n• Level 1: Confessor Cabal & Fast Harrassers (+15% Bike/Buggy/Howitzer speed)\n• Level 2: Cyborg Armor & Raider Buggy Upgrades\n• Level 3: Enlightened, Cyborg Elite & Cyborg Speed Upgrade",
